The CVE-2021-23240 is related to the sudo package, specifically the SELinux-enabled sudoedit. The attack involves a symbolic link attack. The system impacted by this attack is Ubuntu 16.04 ELS. The package version that contains the fix for this vulnerability is sudo-1.8.16-0ubuntu1.11.